  "findings": [
    "NoteTile#getX correctly distinguishes fractional LEFT without live shift, RIGHT with IGNORE_FUTURE_DEACTIVATE, and OVER center; GroupingTile wraps child bounds and PlayingSpace translates full extrema. Rust adds these branches, and all36 original maker note cases recover.",
    "All eight independent recursive/note-side/declaration-order/lifecycle controls fail, typically +30px in height. sequence_lifecycle_layout and attach_sequence_lifecycle_event still reserve SAME_MESSAGE_LIFECYCLE_ROW without an engine parameter, while Java LifeEventTile preferred height is0 except standalone destroy. NoteTile uses event-history level, while Rust still obtains right shifts from ordinate-based legacy segment unions. The source predicates are accounted for but their event histories are not equivalent.",
    "New exo/group and attached-note controls expose additional Teoz origin and component-height dependencies. The22 retained maker life-history failures remain binding. This review does not waive them on the ground that the minX expression alone agrees.",
    "All14 accounts were present byte-for-byte in earlier chronological commits before their corresponding code. See provenance.json and commit-mapping.json. Main release tiers remain11181/11251 product-library and10497/11251 assisted-library; source-only CLI cohort403/955 with10 invalid references; no regressions observed.",
    "Verdict applies to whole source-to-SVG recovery with the dependencies described above. Positive component-local observations are explicitly bounded and are not acceptance. Every mismatch and negative remains in the standing suite."
